# KaamYaab — Real App Transformation Plan

## Summary
Transform KaamYaab from a demo into a real application with Firebase Authentication, role-based signup, user-friendly language, and real booking validation.

## Proposed Changes

---

### 1. New Models & Services

#### [NEW] lib/models/user_model.dart
- `AppUser` with fields: uid, name, phone, city, area, role (customer/worker)
- Worker extras: serviceCategory, skills, baseRatePkr, experienceYears, isAvailable, rating

#### [NEW] lib/services/auth_service.dart
- Firebase Auth with email+password
- Firestore CRUD for customer and worker profiles
- `isWorkerPhoneRegistered(phone)` — validates worker during booking
- Graceful fallback to SharedPreferences if Firebase isn't configured

---

### 2. New Auth Screens

#### [NEW] lib/screens/auth/role_select_screen.dart
- Beautiful landing: two glass cards — "I need a service" (Customer) + "I offer services" (Worker)
- Routes to login or signup based on role

#### [NEW] lib/screens/auth/login_screen.dart
- Phone + password login form
- Role-aware: redirects customer to HomeScreen, worker to ProviderDashboardScreen

#### [NEW] lib/screens/auth/customer_signup_screen.dart
- Fields: Full name, Phone, City (dropdown), Area/Locality, Password

#### [NEW] lib/screens/auth/worker_signup_screen.dart
- Fields: Full name, Phone, City, Service Category (Plumber/Electrician etc.), Skills (chips), Experience, Base Rate (PKR/hr), Password

---

### 3. Routing Updates

#### [MODIFY] lib/screens/splash_screen.dart
- Navigate to `/login` instead of `/home`

#### [MODIFY] lib/main.dart
- Add routes: `/login`, `/signup/customer`, `/signup/worker`
- Auth guard: check if user is logged in before allowing access to home/dashboard

